60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Option A is a flat fee. It covers everything and removes the fear of commitment.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Option B is tiered. It might reduce the workload, but it creates social friction.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Option C is activity-based. It is fair to the regulars, but it kills the casuals.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Option A is the only one that respects the hesitation I saw in the data.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Takumi,,Option A is the only one that covers the fixed costs without constant chasing.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, tiered membership feels like the named-grade years. It caused friction.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, you are right. The minute books show it was a disaster.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shunichi, I agree. Option C is too punishing for the people who come twice a year.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, exactly. The turnout drop proves it. We need a simple entry point.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, I support A. It is the most sustainable for the budget.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I am voting for A. It protects the community feel.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
